Take the default when a number in the config fails to parse

readNumEntry returns QString::toInt() without the success flag. A value
that is not a number reaches the style as zero, not as the shipped
default. A value outside the range of int does the same.

Zero is a live setting for these keys, not an off state. It clears every
check box of the eight keys that carry bit flags. It selects the small
check box for crSize and removes the password character. It makes the
window background fully translucent for bgndOpacity. The next save
writes the lost value back over the file.

Pass the success flag and return the default when the parse fails. An
empty value and an absent key still take the default, as before.

CFG_READ_INT_BOOL reads a key that held a boolean before the option
became a bit mask, and it needs the old pair of tokens. Read true and
false in the macro itself. An old file therefore keeps its meaning, and
a malformed value on the same key now takes the default.

A reader oracle over the fix reads thin=zzqq as 1, crSize=zzz as 15,
gbLabel=zzz as 9, passwordChar=25CF as 9679 and bgndOpacity=2147483648
as 100. Each value is the shipped default, and each read as zero before
the change.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 3 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

